[1.] One line summary of the problem:
Unusually high load average in linux kernel 2.6.35, 2.6.35.1 and later

[2.] Full description of the problem/report:
Whenever I am running X in an affected kernel version, the load average when
the machine is otherwise idle tends to wobble between 0.3 and 1.2 for the
one minute average, and 0.8 or so for the fifteen minute average. (no
programs using cpu, no programs reading/writing to disk, no programs in D
state, no networking ocurring, etc)

[3.] Keywords (i.e., modules, networking, kernel):
kernel X sched
