git bisect log:

# good: [09a40af5240de02d848247ab82440ad75b31ab11] sched: Fix UP update_avg() build warning

[7.] A small shell script or example program which triggers the
     problem (if possible)
Not possible. However, I will instead describe how to easily demonstrate
this problem every time with affected kernels and my machine:

1. Boot and login to X with any programs running.
2. Let the machine idle for ten to twenty minutes so that the initial load
average should settle.
3. If the kernel is working properly, your load average should be pretty
close to zero on all averages. If not, your averages will be closer to
0.3-1.2 for the last minute, and averaging around 0.8 for the rest.

